        "original_id": "036686b1-2045-57b0-8f60-c02a18ee9726",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Raymond Queneau, Peter Straub\n- Organizations: Oulipo\n- Works: A Hundred Thousand Billion Poems\n- Topics: literature, horror fiction, literary awards\n\nFacts:\n- Raymond Queneau was born on 21 February 1903 and died on 25 October 1976.\n- Raymond Queneau was a French novelist, poet, critic, and editor.\n- Raymond Queneau co-founded Oulipo and served as its president.\n- Raymond Queneau was notable for his wit and cynical humour.\n- A Hundred Thousand Billion Poems, originally titled Cent mille milliards de poèmes, is a book by Raymond Queneau that was published in 1961.\n- Peter Francis Straub was born on March 2, 1943.\n- Peter Straub is an American novelist and poet.\n- Peter Straub's horror fiction has received the Bram Stoker Award, the World Fantasy Award, and the International Horror Guild Award.",
